  "changelog": "Initial release.\n\n- Implements Priestley-Taylor and simplified SEBAL methods for regional evapotranspiration (ET, mm/day) estimation from net radiation, air temperature, LST, and NDVI.\n- Outputs include ET raster (GeoTIFF, mm/day, EPSG:4326), summary statistics (JSON), and a manifest.\n- Supports fully offline operation with a synthetic data mode for demonstration and workflow validation.\n- Includes usage examples, input options, and customization (e.g., Priestley-Taylor \u03b1 coefficient).\n- MIT licensed, no external data or network requests required by default.",
